● I posted the plan and task list as a comment on issue #4. I haven't changed
  any code or committed anything, and I'm waiting for your go.

  My recommendation on each open question:

  1. New round reaching History: The list and the high score share one query,
     key ['rounds'], and the high score is derived from the list. useSaveRound
     invalidates that key, without waiting for the refetch before going to the
     result screen.
  2. Delete and the cache: On success, remove ['round', id] and invalidate
     ['rounds']. The detail renders nothing once the delete has succeeded, so it
     can't flash "Could not find this round" while going back. The Result
     screen in the Play tab keeps showing what it had, and "Play again" still
     works. I'll check on the phone what it shows after you delete its round.
  3. Stat display on the detail: Add shared StatCard and TotalCard components.
     The detail shows bars with delay={0}, so they fill together instead of one
     by one, and ScoreBar stays unchanged. TotalCard isn't on your list for
     src/components/, so it needs your OK. Without it the detail builds its own
     total card.
  4. Failed delete: The error text goes under the Delete button with ErrorView's
     "Try again", as in guess.tsx. Try again deletes straight away without
     asking to confirm again.
  5. Date format: toLocaleString('en-GB', …) gives "4 Nov 2026, 14:05", in
     English, in the phone's time zone, and the list and detail use the same
     format. I only checked this output in Node. I'll check it in Expo Go on the
     phone.

  The task list ends with your phone checks. These include the one #3 left open:
  play a round, fully close Expo Go, reopen it, and see that History shows that
  round with its real data. I'll cover the loading and error states by reading
  the code, since they're hard to trigger on a phone.

